--------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. DATAPACKS ARE FREE
--------------------------------------------------------------------------
Everything under the Mod's `data/` folders (class, subclass, branch, race
and ability definitions, loot tables, tags, damage types and any other
datapack content) is free to use. You may edit it, delete it, replace it
and create new datapack content for the Mod, and you may share and sell
the datapacks you create. This applies to datapacks you write yourself;
it does not give you the right to redistribute the Mod's compiled code
or its non-datapack assets (see section 4).

--------------------------------------------------------------------------
2. USE IN MODPACKS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------
You may include the unmodified Mod in a modpack, and play, stream and
record it, provided that:
  a) the Author is credited (name of the Mod and name of the Author) in
     the modpack's description or credits page, with a link to the Mod's
     official page;
  b) the Mod is not modified, and is obtained from an official
     distribution page of the Author (see section 4);
  c) the modpack and any server or service using the Mod comply with
     section 3.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------
3. PROHIBITED USES
--------------------------------------------------------------------------
The Mod, and any modpack, server, addon or service that uses it, must NOT
be used in or for:
  a) Pay-to-win: selling or granting, in exchange for money or any other
     real-world consideration, any gameplay advantage related to the Mod,
     including classes, races, class or race ranks, experience, skill
     points, resets, abilities, gear, items, mana, stats or any other
     progression or power.
  b) Pay-to-fast: selling or granting, in exchange for real-world
     consideration, faster progression, skipped content (for example
     skipped rites or requirements), boosts or time savers related to the
     Mod.
  c) Any server, community, modpack or distribution that discriminates
     against people on the basis of race, ethnicity, nationality,
     religion, sex, gender, sexual orientation, disability, age or any
     similar characteristic, or that promotes hatred or harassment.
  d) Any malicious purpose, including malware, data theft or the
     deliberate harm of other people's computers, accounts or servers.
Purely cosmetic items that give no gameplay advantage are not covered by
(a) and (b).

--------------------------------------------------------------------------
4. REDISTRIBUTION AND MODIFICATION
--------------------------------------------------------------------------
Except as stated in sections 1, 2 and 5, you may NOT:
  a) upload, mirror or redistribute the Mod, in whole or in part, in
     modified or unmodified form, on any site or service, whether or not
     for money;
  b) sell, rent or charge for the Mod or for access to it, including
     through ad-links, paywalls or donation-gated downloads;
  c) modify, decompile, re-package or copy the Mod's code or non-datapack
     assets into another project.
The official distribution pages are those the Author lists in the Mod's
repository or project description.
Modpack distribution platforms (for example CurseForge, Modrinth or
launcher-managed pack files) may download the Mod from its official page
as part of installing a modpack that complies with section 2.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------
5. ADDONS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------
You may create addons that add classes, subclasses, races, abilities,
rites or other content to the Mod, whether as datapacks or as separate
mods that depend on the Mod through its published interfaces. Addons may
be sold or monetized, and may use any license of their choice, provided
that:
  a) the addon does not contain a copy of the Mod's code, textures or
     other non-datapack assets;
  b) the addon complies with section 3 (in particular, an addon cannot be
     sold as, or give access to, a pay-to-win or pay-to-fast advantage);
  c) the addon does not present itself as an official part of the Mod.

